        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rei Kawakubo, Adrian Joffe\n- Companies: Dover Street Market, Comme des Garçons\n- Products: Ann Demeulemeester, Balenciaga, Céline, Gucci, Hussein Chalayan, Junya Watanabe, J.W.Anderson, Lanvin, LOEWE, Maison Margiela, Marni\n- Concepts: Japanese fashion label, high fashion brands\n\nFacts:\n- Comme des Garçons is a Japanese fashion label founded by and headed by Rei Kawakubo.\n- Comme des Garçons means “like boys” in French.\n- Dover Street Market was created by Rei Kawakubo of Comme des Garçons and her husband Adrian Joffe.\n- Dover Street Market sells Comme des Garçons and complementary high fashion brands including Ann Demeulemeester, Balenciaga, Céline, Gucci, Hussein Chalayan, Junya Watanabe, J.W.Anderson, Lanvin, LOEWE, Maison Margiela, and Marni.",
